          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "High blood pressure, or essential hypertension (I10), is classified in Chapter 9 of ICD-10-CM, which covers diseases of the circulatory system. This is found in the hypertensive-disease block, I10 to I16, as stated in the document \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family\".\n\nChapter 9 deliberately excludes:\n*   Circulatory disorders that complicate pregnancy or childbirth, which are classified in the obstetric chapter.\n*   Giant cell arteritis and systemic vasculitides, which are classified with connective-tissue disorders in the musculoskeletal chapter.\n*   Symptoms such as chest pain, palpitations, abnormal cardiac findings, and elevated blood pressure readings in individuals without a diagnosis. These remain in Chapter 18 (symptoms, signs and abnormal findings) until a diagnosis is recorded.\n\nThis information is from the document \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 9: diseases of the circulatory system (I00-I99)\".\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
